WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:04.183
(slow orchestral music)

00:00:08.006 --> 00:00:10.256
(laughter)

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.441
- [Narrator] I was in a
show which was the most

00:00:13.441 --> 00:00:15.937
popular show ever in
the former Yugoslavia.

00:00:15.937 --> 00:00:17.601
(laughter)

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:20.763
Imagine we had over two and
a half million audience live.

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:23.013
(laughter)

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:28.036
Being popular like that you can
not even walk on the street.

00:00:29.027 --> 00:00:30.581
My name is Jasmin Geljo,

00:00:30.581 --> 00:00:32.016
and I'm an actor.

00:00:32.016 --> 00:00:34.567
I came as a refugee in 1993

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.400
to escape

00:00:36.509 --> 00:00:38.092
the war over there.

00:00:41.945 --> 00:00:44.385
I love my profession.

00:00:44.385 --> 00:00:46.718
I like to make people happy.

00:00:48.046 --> 00:00:49.155
When I came to Canada

00:00:49.155 --> 00:00:52.674
I realized I didn't have
the tools to be an actor

00:00:52.674 --> 00:00:55.662
cause I didn't speak English.

00:00:55.662 --> 00:00:57.659
You have to survive
somehow, you have to work.

00:00:57.659 --> 00:01:01.098
I was working so many
different type of job.

00:01:01.098 --> 00:01:03.982
When I was a salesperson
like knocking door to door

00:01:03.982 --> 00:01:06.534
trying to sell perfumes,

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:08.863
I was recognized as an actor

00:01:08.863 --> 00:01:10.749
by people from former Yugoslavia,

00:01:10.749 --> 00:01:13.079
but I didn't want to speak my own language

00:01:13.079 --> 00:01:16.629
because I was so ashamed for them

00:01:16.629 --> 00:01:19.457
to see me in that kind of position.

00:01:19.457 --> 00:01:22.290
Being somebody and dropping really

00:01:23.236 --> 00:01:24.653
to become nobody.

00:01:25.989 --> 00:01:28.541
(piano music)

00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:31.979
I learned English by
listening to other people.

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:35.086
And started auditioning, I found agent and

00:01:35.086 --> 00:01:38.913
small part by small part, I, you know,

00:01:38.913 --> 00:01:41.298
I start working my profession again.

00:01:41.298 --> 00:01:42.296
Two thousand dollars.

00:01:42.296 --> 00:01:43.184
- Oh.

00:01:43.184 --> 00:01:44.238
- Best I can do.

00:01:44.238 --> 00:01:46.345
Being an actor with an accent,

00:01:46.345 --> 00:01:49.174
I always play the worst character

00:01:49.174 --> 00:01:50.433
in the film.

00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:53.445
But believe me, I'm good,
I'm a very good person.

00:01:53.445 --> 00:01:55.695
(laughter)

00:01:56.607 --> 00:01:58.857
In 2016 I was nominate for

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.431
Canadian Screen Award as a

00:02:02.431 --> 00:02:06.036
best lead actor in a feature film.

00:02:06.036 --> 00:02:10.770
I was like thinking of when
you go back 20 years ago,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:14.375
being nobody and now being nominated,

00:02:14.375 --> 00:02:15.983
it's really,

00:02:15.983 --> 00:02:17.209
nice feelings.

00:02:17.209 --> 00:02:19.709
(piano music)

